**Figure 1** (`fig1_pilot_chi_c.png/pdf`). Pilot, L = 64, seeds 1 and 2, 20,000 sweeps: susceptibility chi (log axis) and heat capacity c per site against T. Both peak at T = 2.30 on the grid (chi parabola refinement 2.307), about 0.04 above the exact T_c = 2.2692 (red dashed), the expected finite-size shift. Grey: stage-2 window. Seed-to-seed spread is mostly smaller than the markers.

**Figure 2** (`fig2_binder.png/pdf`). Binder cumulant U against T. L = 32, 64, 128 (stage 2, pooled over 3 seeds, block-bootstrap error bars) cross at T_c = 2.2759 (dotted), 95% seed-bootstrap interval [2.2708, 2.2810] (band), exact T_c 2.2692 (red dashed) lies just outside it. Open squares: L = 256 at 10^4 sweeps, not equilibrated, error bars underestimated; they scatter far from the crossing. Filled diamonds: equilibrated L = 256 supplement (5x10^4 burn-in + 5x10^4 sweeps); they are consistent with the stage-2 curves at T <= 2.261, but at T >= 2.276 they have large errors (e.g. U = 0.37 +- 0.11 at 2.276 against about 0.60 at the crossing), so they constrain T_c only loosely. Thin lines in the left panel: stage-2 scaling fit.
